My high school athletic career unfortunately came to an end last Friday with a 31-38 loss to Bishop Chatard in the 4A sectional semifinals. It was a tough loss but our team never gave up and has a lot to be proud of. My last time on the field was with a successful 44 yard FG with 7 minutes left in the game. 

Between football and soccer, I played 27 games in 11 weeks this season. Thank you to my family who was at every single game. 

⚽️It is hard to say goodbye to a sport that I’ve played basically my whole life.   I am thankful for all the coaches, teammates, and memories I have had through school and travel ball. 

🏈 What a ride! Thank you to my Northview teammates, coaches, and community. I’m grateful for every minute spent on the field. 

🏈I’m not ready to end this chapter. I’m ready to put in more work and step up to the next level. I’m looking for my next home. I’ve consistently improved over four years and ended with 264 career points. I know there’s still plenty of room to grow and improve, but I also feel that I have a lot to offer to a college team. 

Season and career stats coming soon! Looking forward to putting in more work during the off season. 

